<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Culloden</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1746">1746</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Culloden · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacobite-rising-of-1745">Jacobite rising of 1745</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Culloden was fought on 16 April 1746 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inverness">Inverness</a>, where the government army under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ernest-augustus-king-of-hanover">Duke of Cumberland</a> destroyed the Jacobite army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-edward-stuart">Charles Edward Stuart</a> in less than an hour. It was the last pitched battle fought on British soil. Harsh repression followed, and laws against Highland dress, arms and hereditary jurisdictions broke the power of the clans.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-culloden.jpg" alt="Battle of Culloden" width="320" height="193" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: David Morier · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Battle_of_Culloden.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Jacobite risings in support of the exiled Stuarts were defeated in 1715 and in 1745–1746, when Charles Edward Stuart reached Derby before his army was destroyed at the <b>Battle of Culloden</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-great-britain">Kingdom of Great Britain · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>…flight of Prince Charles Edward Stuart, &quot;Bonnie Prince Charlie&quot;, from Benbecula to the Isle of Skye as he evaded government soldiers after his defeat at the <b>Battle of Culloden</b> in 1746: disguised as a serving maid, he escaped in a small boat with the help of Flora MacDonald.</blockquote><a href="/songs/the-skye-boat-song">The Skye Boat Song</a></li><li><blockquote>The rising ended at <b>Culloden</b> in April 1746.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/december-6">6 December in history</a></li><li><blockquote>The Jacobite rising he launched ended in defeat at <b>Culloden</b> in April 1746.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/july-23">23 July in history</a></li></ul></section>
